WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.851
This page is one Observation —
a record of a URL, a region, and a time.

00:00:04.851 --> 00:00:08.921
Observation details is the title.
Back to list returns to the table.

00:00:08.921 --> 00:00:13.367
Captured and Region are facts from this run.
Requested and Observed stay separate.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.608
The URL is the address that was captured.

00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:21.369
Status is the capture outcome:
Success, Failure, or Pending — not a page verdict.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:24.516
The screenshot is what rendered
at capture time from that region.

00:00:24.516 --> 00:00:28.636
This is a record, not a delivery promise
and not ad-tag verification.

00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:34.557
The same capture also stores title,
description, canonical, robots, and Open Graph.

00:00:34.557 --> 00:00:40.882
Page Signals is an indicative score from
stored html_signals, always with reasons. It is not Observed.

00:00:40.882 --> 00:00:45.386
Compare and Share use records you already have.
They do not start a new capture.

00:00:45.386 --> 00:00:49.601
The confirmation record seal shows
the record ID and the server record time.

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:53.441
Image check fingerprint and page data
check code stay on this record.

00:00:53.441 --> 00:00:59.087
Visual similarity is a reference only.
The seal is not third-party verification or formal proof.

00:00:59.087 --> 00:01:03.132
Monitoring on Starter and Pro recaptures
this URL and region on a schedule.

00:01:03.132 --> 00:01:06.740
Each scheduled run uses one Observation
from the monthly allowance.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.545
Share and CSV export existing records.
They do not start a new capture.

00:01:11.545 --> 00:01:17.817
Screenshots are removed after the plan window.
URL, region, and time metadata remain.

